From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: a large depth image whose guest bytes are all zero is cleared to zero instead of uploaded (EDEN_UP_BIG_DEPTH_NO_UPLOAD=<MiB>), off by default

What: EDEN_UP_BIG_IMAGE_LOG shows Ocarina's 12288x12288 D16 shadow map made by JoinImages with
rt=0 (first seen as a texture, not as a cleared or drawn target) and uploaded from guest memory
right there: "staging=288MiB went through", at the area load where the pool is empty. JoinImages'
last branch calls RefreshContents for every new image that no clear, whole join copy or drawn-over
target covers, and RefreshContents uploads whatever guest memory holds.

With EDEN_UP_BIG_DEPTH_NO_UPLOAD=<MiB> (digits, 1..65536, read once; test value 128),
RefreshContents first reads the guest bytes of a depth or depth-stencil image of at least that
size (plain only: not sparse, unbacked, converted, rescaled, MSAA or with dirty layers), page by
page as MemoryManager::ReadBlockImpl does (a page without memory reads zero, a page the front will
not hand out as a span is copied through GuestReadThrough). Every byte zero: the image is cleared
with vkCmdClearDepthStencilImage to depth 0.0 / stencil 0, which are the texels an upload of zero
bytes gives in any tiling; no staging, no unswizzle, no buffer-to-image copy. One non-zero byte: the
upload runs as before. Applies to every RefreshContents of such an image, so a later CPU write that
marks it modified again is handled the same way (zero: clear; data: upload): the skip does not
move the upload. Tracking (TrackImage) and CpuModified are handled as before, at the top.

Lines (HW_GPU, the first 16 then powers of two, each kind counted apart):
"EDEN_UP_BIG_DEPTH: cleared instead of uploaded ... staging_avoided=<MiB> no_memory_pages=<n>
scan=<ms> ... (<n> cleared, <MiB> of staging avoided so far; <n> kept)",
"EDEN_UP_BIG_DEPTH: kept the upload ... a non-zero byte at +<offset> scan=<ms>",
"EDEN_UP_BIG_DEPTH: not checked ... flags=<hex> ...: uploaded".

Also: vkCmdClearDepthStencilImage in the Vulkan wrapper (loaded with the other device functions),
TextureCacheRuntime::ClearDepthToZero.

Off: one compare per upload. Not in the kept-store stamp: texture_cache*.h, vk_texture_cache.*
and vulkan_wrapper.* are not translation inputs; no switch name added to TranslationSwitches.
---
